---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const direct = `const status = await connect.checkDirectAccess();

if (status === "permission_required") {
  directAccessButton.onclick = async () => {
    await connect.requestDirectAccess();
  };
}

connect.onConnectionChange((connection) => {
  // "direct", "relay", or "hosted"
  renderRoute(connection?.route);
});`;

const options = `const connect = new MdbaseConnect({
  serverUrl: "https://connect.mdbase.dev",
  manifest,
  redirectUri,
  directAccess: "auto",
  relayEncryption: "required"
});`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Local and hosted routes"
  description="Let the SDK select direct, encrypted relay, or hosted-provider transport while your feature code stays on one operation interface."
  active="routing"
  headings={[
    { href: "#automatic", label: "Automatic routing" },
    { href: "#direct", label: "Direct access" },
    { href: "#relay", label: "Encrypted relay" },
    { href: "#hosted", label: "Hosted provider" },
    { href: "#native", label: "Native shells" }
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="automatic">Route selection is not a storage mode</h2>
  <p>
    A collection has one write authority: either a local connector for a
    filesystem folder or a hosted provider. For a local authority, the SDK
    prefers the fixed same-computer endpoint and falls back to the encrypted
    relay. The user chooses where the collection lives, not which network route
    an individual request takes.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={options} language="ts" label="connect-options.ts" />

  <h2 id="direct">Request same-computer browser access from a user gesture</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={direct} language="ts" label="direct-access.ts" />
  <p>
    Browser local-network permission must be requested from a user action. Once
    available, grantable operations prefer
    <code>http://127.0.0.1:28485/v1/operations</code>. The connector checks the
    exact origin, Host header, protocol version, grant, and application-key
    proof.
  </p>
  <p>
    Set <code>directAccess: "disabled"</code> only when the embedding
    environment cannot make loopback requests.
  </p>

  <h2 id="relay">Encrypted relay fallback</h2>
  <p>
    Protocol 1 uses a non-extractable P-256 key and atomic message counter in
    IndexedDB. The SDK encrypts operation inputs for the local connector and
    decrypts results in the application. The control plane routes opaque bodies
    while retaining operation and delivery metadata.
  </p>
  <p>
    New authorizations require encrypted relay by default. An encrypted grant
    never falls back to plaintext. Use
    <code>relayEncryption: "disabled"</code> only against a development stack
    that intentionally lacks end-to-end relay encryption.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosted">Hosted-provider route</h2>
  <p>
    Authorization for a hosted collection returns a short-lived,
    grant-bound provider capability. The SDK sends operations directly to the
    provider, binds browser requests to the approved callback origin, and
    refreshes that capability as needed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Record payloads do not pass through the Connect control plane. The hosted
    provider can decrypt records because it must execute canonical mdbase
    operations. Treat it as a trusted data processor, not as zero-knowledge
    storage.
  </p>

  <h2 id="native">Native shells</h2>
  <p>
    Supply <code>navigate</code> to open authorization in the system browser,
    list a private-use callback scheme in the bundled manifest, and provide the
    received deep link to <code>completeAuthorization(callbackUrl)</code>.
    Native shells may also supply custom authorization storage and grant key
    stores.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>

